<title>BRAZIL: Raytheon unconcerned by Brazil probe.</title>
<headline>Raytheon unconcerned by Brazil probe.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. high-technology giant Raytheon Co said Thursday it saw no reason to be concerned about a Brazilian probe into a $1.4 billion project for an Amazonian radar surveillance system.</p>
<p>Barry French, Raytheon's director of international public affairs, told Reuters the company had not yet taken a close look at a decision by the government's financial watchdog to ask public prosecutors to investigate the project.</p>
<p>&quot;Our first reaction was essentially that there didn't seem to be any surprises that we should be concerned about,&quot; French said by telephone from Raytheon's Rio de Janeiro office.</p>
</text>
